-- title:
--   Distinctness of the two branch coordinates u ≠ v
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi \in W$. Consider the ring of formal power series in two variables `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W`, whose variables are `MvPowerSeries.X 0` and `MvPowerSeries.X 1`, and the principal ideal `uvCrossingIdeal W π` generated by the single element $X_0X_1 - \pi$, where $\pi$ is viewed as a constant power series; the quotient by this ideal is the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W π`, i.e. $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$. Assume that the quotient $W/(\pi)$ of $W$ by the principal ideal generated by $\pi$ is nontrivial, i.e. $\pi$ is not a unit of $W$ (so in particular $W$ itself is nontrivial). The conclusion is that the two elements `U π` and `V π` of the crossing model — the two branch coordinates, the images of the two power series variables — are distinct elements of that ring.
--
--   This is the elementary separation statement underlying the branch-exchange involution $u \leftrightarrow v$ of the local model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ for an ordinary double point: the involution is not the identity as soon as $\pi$ fails to be a unit. It is used in the analysis of the fixed subring of that involution, via [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.U_notMem_fixedSubring`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.U_notMem_fixedSubring); for $W$ the Witt vectors of $\overline{\mathbb F}_p$ and $\pi = p$ the ring is the local model at a supersingular point of the $\Gamma_0(p)$-moduli problem in characteristic $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_U_ne_V.lean

